# Walkthrough: MTG UI Modernization

I have successfully updated the Magic: The Gathering (MTG) section to match the premium, professional design system we established for the Pokémon category. This ensures a consistent, high-end experience regardless of which TCG a user is browsing.

## Changes Made

### [MTG Card Detail](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/store/view_mtg_card.php)
-   **Premium White Panel**: Replaced the previous layout with the new high-contrast white product container, complete with a professional 60px drop-shadow.
-   **Integrated Typography**: Realigned the card name, rarity badge, and set info to create a clean, modern header inside the panel.
-   **Unified Action Bar**:
    -   Aligned the quantity stepper and the "Add to Shopping Bag" button on the same line.
    -   Unified both elements to a solid **60px height**.
-   **80px Pricing Gap**: Implemented the clear horizontal separation between the Shop Price and the Scryfall live market data.

### [MTG Category Alignment](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/store/magic_index.php)
-   **Stable Breadcrumbs**: Standardized the breadcrumb wrapper padding to `px-4 px-md-5` across the Category Landing and Set pages.
-   **Visual Synchronization**: Navigation now stays perfectly static when moving from an MTG Set list into an individual MTG Card.

